A retype takes the Untyped's first block of the size whatever it made before,
so two things it made claim the same memory,
and a frame may be mapped over a pool.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: memory that may hold kernel objects overlaps a node not above or below it

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -211,7 +211,7 @@ static int op_untyped(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
          * Everything this Untyped made lies below the watermark, so the block overlaps none of it.
          * The mark is at most the size and the size a multiple of len, so nothing wraps.
          */
-        uint32_t off = (untyped_mark(u) + len - 1) & ~(len - 1);
+        uint32_t off = 0;
         if (off > size - len) {
             return KERR_NO_MEMORY;
         }
